	url = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85030222518&doi=10.1109%2fELECTRONICS.2017.7995225&partnerID=40&md5=38f552f61065453ca09dfccc3ab2ea80},
	doi = {10.1109/ELECTRONICS.2017.7995225},
	abstract = {Load modelling is an essential instrument to carry through the planning for modern power system with widely access of renewable energy generation ({REG}). And it is necessary to analyse the potential growth activity of {REG} for {CO}2 reduction. Aiming at raising the scale of {REG} in final consumption segment, this paper presents the analysis of substitution effect among different kinds of energy. Within the strict constraint of energy balance and end-use efficiency by analogy to the efficiency function of Well-to-Wheel ({WTW}), this paper establishes a multi-objective optimized load model focusing on rebuilding an economic and environmental friendly structure of final energy consumption. Bi-level optimization is used to solve the model. 0bjective of the main-problem aims at system economy considering {CO}2 emission, while the sub- problem with objective denoting to maximize the scale of alternative {REG} power consumption. Finally, to improve the {REG} utilization in the whole process from generation to consumption, a concept of flexible load curve combination and its relative capability of raising the renewable energy resource integration is proposed based on generalized energy storage. © 2017 {IEEE}.},
