	abstract = {Providing end-users with a variety of energy products‚ energy system with multi-energy complementary integration can improve the comprehensive energy utilization efficiency and reduce carbon emission. This paper studies the structural design and optimal configuration method of the modular prefabricated integrated energy cabinet. According to different types of energy supply‚ the integrated energy cabinet is divided into an electric energy zone and a heating and cooling zone. A mathematical model of the main equipment installed in the integrated energy container is established. An optimal allocation model is developed based on the mixed-integer nonlinear programming method. The 着-constraint method is adopted to solve the multi-objective optimization problem‚ and the multi-objective decision-making method based on Euclidean distance is used to obtain the final optimal solution to decide an optimal allocation scheme of integrated energy. © 2021 Editorial Department of Zhejiang Electric Power. All rights reserved.},
