	abstract = {To determine the location and configuration for energy storage plants, this work establishes the optimization method of energy storage plants based on the energy balance and constraints. This is applicable for the location selection and capacity determination. Firstly, the location is pre-selected considering load, installed capacity of renewable energy, and average distance of neighboring nodes. The location and configuration of the plants are optimized through the multi-objective artificial bee colony algorithm with maximizing the peak-shaving profit, minimizing the investment cost and active network loss as evaluation indicators. The tide calculation is performed with the lowest operating cost as the objective, and the hourly optimal charging and discharging power are optimized. The results show that the proposed method can effectively realize the optimization of location and capacity for energy storage plants, and the renewable energy utilization can be promoted.  © 2023 {IEEE}.},
