	title = {Multi-Objective Optimal Dispatch of Smart Grid by Estimating Available Capacity of {EV} Aggregators},
	isbn = {978-1-6654-1439-5},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85128073348&doi=10.1109%2fiSPEC53008.2021.9735894&partnerID=40&md5=06c0dc7758f15b428d887b29af696557},
	doi = {10.1109/iSPEC53008.2021.9735894},
	abstract = {In recent decade, the vehicle to grid (V2G) technology makes the electric vehicles ({EVs}) become the potential energy storage capacity for alleviating the random fluctuation of the renewable energy power. The {EV} aggregator is the promising solution to aggregate enough capacity for the V2G. In this paper, a preliminary study of the multi-objective optimal dispatch of smart grid by estimating available capacity of {EV} aggregators is proposed. The behavior of {EVs} is described by a statistical model to estimate the maximum available capacity of {EVs}. Then, the multi-objectives and constrains are defined for the multi-objective optimal dispatch. The multi-objective genetic particle swarm optimizer is used to solve the high dimensional multi-objective optimization problem to obtain the Pareto front. The multi-objective optimization results show that the charging period of {EVs} is shifted to avoid load peak for the solved optimal dispatch. © 2021 {IEEE}.},
