	abstract = {To enable renewable energy sources ({RES}) to better and more efficiently assist traditional generators in attending the automatic generation control ({AGC}), firstly, renewable energy power plants and energy storage systems ({ESSs}) are formed as the aggregated generation unit ({AGU}). Secondly, a real-time mesh adaptive multi-objective optimization algorithm ({MA}-{MO}) calculation is proposed. The proposed algorithm combines the real-time simulation and {MA}-{MO} results based on the future load disturbance prediction data. Then the optimal allocation ratio of {AGC} instructions is calculated for the 1-minute-ahead operation of the traditional generator and {AGU}, improving the {AGC} performance with the minimum system frequency deviation and smoothing the state of charge ({SoC}) of {ESS}. Finally, the proposed optimization algorithm is verified based on the simulation of a field {AGU} system. © 2023 {IEEE}.},
