	doi = {10.1109/SPAC53836.2021.9539917},
	abstract = {Hybrid renewable energy system ({HRES}) is a promising way to promote the supply stability of renewable energy and reduce carbon emission. This paper focuses on designing a novel {HRES} with equipment type consideration. Multiple types of equipment can improve the flexibility and reliability of the {HRES}, meanwhile more types means higher investment and maintenance cost. The optimization of such system involves a large number of discrete variables and complex performance equations. To deal with this problem, A two-step approach is proposed in this study. The minimum total annual cost and minimum equipment types are set as the optimization goals. A group of Pareto sets are generated after optimization process. These results can help engineers evaluate the impact of multiple factors and assist them in decision-making. © 2021 {IEEE}.},
