	abstract = {Distributed energy storage ({DES}) systems have become a promising technology that can address challenges related to intermittent renewable energy, grid stability, and demand fluctuations. This article first describes different forms of distributed energy storage and generation systems, and compares and analyzes them in terms of scale, layout, configuration, and application. Due to the significant differences in the implementation methods of distributed energy storage power generation based on different principles, the above factors should be fully considered when applying. The designed {DES} system needs to be integrated with the distribution network, so this paper introduces the committed steps of the integration of the {DES} system and the distribution network, then sorts out the commonly used optimization goals of {DES} integration, such as cost minimization, peak shaving, emission reduction and multi-objective optimization, and finally gives the mainstream algorithm of the basic optimization of the {DES} system. The {DES} system can enhance grid flexibility, improve renewable energy utilization, and help establish more sustainable and resilient energy infrastructure. © 2023 {IEEE}.},
