	isbn = {18033814},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84938068828&partnerID=40&md5=67bfdd66277025a81a8d62c9ae78af17},
	abstract = {As strong concerns about the environmental risks and the future availability of fossil fuels exist, there is wide consensus on the need to increase the exploitation of renewable energies, possibly to reach the maximum share within energy systems. An important question is identified: which is the possible composition of a sustainable energy scenario. The search for a reasonable integration criterion of renewable energies will be treated as a multi-objective optimization problem, for which we develop a mutation operator based on domain knowledge of the energy sector. The mutation is tested on a real world problem, and found that it can converge to optimal Pareto-set more efficiently than generic mutation.},
