	abstract = {Hybrid Energy Systems ({HESs}) are becoming popular for standalone applications due to price volatility of fossil fuel resources and global concern on {GHG} emission. Expansion of an existing standalone Internal Combustion Generator ({ICG}) system while incorporating renewable energy sources is taken in to discussion in this work which converts {ICG} systems into a {HES}. In order to achieve this, a standalone {HES} consisting of wind turbines, {SPV} panels, batter bank, {ICG} and bi-directional converters is mathematically modeled, simulated and optimized considering power supply reliability, Levelized Energy Cost ({LEC}) and Renewable Energy Capacity ({REC}). Obtained Pareto fronts were analyzed and simple multi-criterion decision making technique is used to come up with the final system design.},
