	abstract = {An approach is proposed to evaluate various micro-grid hybrid electric system configuration possibilities, in terms of installed capacity of different conversion technologies. A multi-objective optimization algorithm (hybrid Multi-Objective Genetic Algorithm) has been applied to determine the Pareto front of optimal trade-off solutions, which compete between a low environmental impact and a cost-effective system. As a case study, the method has been applied to the electric market of Porto Santo Island, where currently existing conventional and renewable electricity generation forms (thermoelectric, onshore wind and solar {PV}) have been evaluated together with new forms of marine energy (waves and offshore wind). The optimization problem is subjected to linear and non-linear constrains related with the minimum supply of the islands’ electric demand, a minimum renewable energy factor, and an established limit of {CO}2 emissions. © 2023 the Author(s).},
