	title = {An Optimal Dispatch Strategy for A Distributed Microgrid Using Snake Optimizer},
	isbn = {978-1-6654-5215-1},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85166389835&doi=10.1109%2fICCSIE55183.2023.10175294&partnerID=40&md5=760656fbf5957323a64f4b3f8866d10b},
	doi = {10.1109/ICCSIE55183.2023.10175294},
	abstract = {In this paper, we propose an optimal scheduling strategy, which is to reduce the operating costs of microgrids while using as much clean energy as possible. Therefore, this paper uses a new metaheuristics algorithm, Snake Optimizer({SO}), solves a multi-objective optimization model for microgrids. The algorithm simulates the behavior and patterns of snake foraging and reproduction, and allocates the population into two groups of males and females according to certain rules. In turn, population renewal strategies are generated based on the specific mating behavior of snakes. Based on the comparison of the two search results, it is proved that the algorithm has strong global search capability and good robustness of convergence results. In addition, the proposed optimization strategy is applicable to all operating modes of the microgrid. {SO} improves the ability of microgrids to operate independently while reducing the cost of microgrid generation. In the process of finding the optimal dispatching strategy in microgrid operation, for the multi-objective optimization problem of microgrid, the traditional intelligent optimization algorithm is easy to fall into the local optimal solution, which makes it difficult to find the global optimal solution. © 2023 {IEEE}.},
